From: Uke Linux maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: admit Uke camera power rails

The rear OV13B10 and front OV08D10 sensors require three additional
power rails not previously admitted by the RPMH regulator driver:
ldob20 (cam_vio 1.8V, shared DOVDD), ldoe6 (rear cam_vdig 1.2V),
and ldoc3 (front cam_vdig 1.2V). Extend the allow-list accordingly.

Signed-off-by: Uke Linux maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c b/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator-uke.c
@@ -2014,7 +2014,10 @@
     strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldob12") &&
     strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldod3") &&
-    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "bobb1")
+    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "bobb1") &&
+    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldob20") &&
+    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldoe6") &&
+    strcmp(aggr_vreg->resource_name, "ldoc3")
    return -ENODEV;

    aggr_vreg->addr = cmd_db_read_addr(aggr_vreg->resource_name);
